https://doi.org/10.5194/egusphere-egu26-1927
  > # Differentiable Atmospheric Modelling with SpeedyWeather.jl

Published: 2026-03-13. 0 citations.

## Abstract

The current generation of hybrid machine learning and physics-informed machine learning is often limited by the missing availability of comprehensive differentiable models: either strongly simplified models have to be used or machine learning (ML) can’t be integrated natively into process-based models and must be trained separately. Here, we present the ongoing development of SpeedyWeather.jl: A general circulation model that’s differentiable, GPU-capable and ready for ML simulations

